[[File:Safespot Gargoyle Slayer Tower.png|thumb|A player standing at the east side of the adjacent bookcase as a safespot.]]
[[Gargoyle]]s can be assigned as a [[Slayer task]] by various [[Slayer masters]] at level 75 [[Slayer]], level 80 [[Combat level|combat]], and with completion of the [[Priest in Peril]] [[quest]]. They are only found in the [[Slayer Tower]], either on the top floor or in the basement. The gargoyles in the basement of the Slayer Tower can only be killed while on a Slayer task, as [[Raulyn]] will stop the player if they attempt to fight them off-task. Gargoyles have a [[Superior slayer monster]] variant, the level 349 [[marble gargoyle]]. Unlike regular gargoyles, the marble gargoyle also utilises ranged attacks. It also has a special attack, launching a white-red orb that deals heavy damage and entraps the player if not dodged; this attack has a 1x1 AoE (in other words, it affects only the single tile where the player was standing). 

Gargoyles are weak to both magic and crush attacks, but melee is commonly used due to the lack of safespots, less defence against their attacks and expenses for casting spells. They have -2 [[flat armour]], so weapons such as [[Dual macuahuitl]] are recommended to make use of the extra damage. Even then, they are still easily fought with most standard weapons one might have available.

To kill a gargoyle, a [[rock hammer]], a [[rock thrownhammer]], or a [[granite hammer]] must be used when they reach 9 or lower [[Hitpoints]]. Normally, the item must be used on the gargoyle, but players can buy the "Gargoyle Smasher" perk from [[Slayer master]]s for 120 [[Slayer points]], which will automatically smash the gargoyle when it falls to 9 or lower Hitpoints, provided that the player has a rock hammer (or equivalent) in their inventory. The granite hammer will automatically smash gargoyles even without the perk if it is equipped. The [[rock hammer]] is faster than the [[rock thrownhammer]] as it does not have travel time. If both are in the inventory, the rock hammer is used in melee distance, while thrownhammers are used outside of melee distance.

Gargoyles also have a boss variant, the [[Grotesque Guardians]]. In order to access them, the player must kill gargoyles on-task to obtain the [[brittle key]], which unlocks the boss arena. The boss fight consists of two gargoyles; [[Dusk]] and [[Dawn]]. Players can choose between melee and a melee/range hybrid; the former requires a [[polearms|polearm]] weapon, while the latter has easier accessibility. 

When considering whether to kill regular gargoyles or the Grotesque Guardians, it is worth noting that the normal gargoyles are much faster to kill and require less supplies and effort, whereas the Grotesque Guardians are more time-consuming, and require more effort and supplies to kill. The requirements for killing the Guardians are also substantially higher in terms of stats and gear. The drop table of the Guardians is not significantly better than gargoyles, especially considering that regular gargoyles have very decent drops as well. However, the Guardians are one of only two sources of [[granite dust]], which is untradeable. The dust strengthens steel cannonballs, turning them into [[granite cannonball]]s with a max hit of 35 instead of 30.

It is recommended to kill gargoyles in the basement during a task, as there are many gargoyles in a fairly small area compared to the top floor. The basement is also large enough that the player can reset the aggression timer easily without leaving the area.

If killing the [[Grotesque Guardians]], it is strongly recommended the player avoid purchasing '''Double Trouble''', as this causes the boss to be counted as two kills per task rather than one, drastically reducing the amount of kills per task.

